  <Properties>
    <pitchId>
      <Value><![CDATA[tinder-for-horses]]></Value>
    </pitchId>
    <title>
      <Value><![CDATA[Tinder for Horses]]></Value>
    </title>
    <tagline>
      <Value><![CDATA[Swipe right. Finally, a stable relationship.]]></Value>
    </tagline>
    <demoFeatures>
      <Value><![CDATA[Swipe Hoof
Stable Match
Neigh Chat
Hay Premium]]></Value>
    </demoFeatures>
    <cardsEpic>
      <Value><![CDATA[Global horse onboarding | Every horse on Earth signed up by Q2. Legal asks if a hoof can accept terms and conditions.
Series A, funded in oats | Investors want traction. Horses have traction, on grass. Legal says it does not count.
Single Sign-On for horses | One hoof, one login. Security wants two-factor. The horse has four factors and no thumbs.
Expand to ponies | Same codebase, smaller viewport. Sales estimated it as 'basically free'.
AI-powered chemistry engine | Predicts true love from mane volume and oat preference. Training data: four horses from Jutland.
Monetise the stable | Freemium for foals, enterprise for dressage horses. The pricing page just says 'Call us'.]]></Value>
    </cardsEpic>
    <cardsStory>
      <Value><![CDATA[Swipe left on geldings | As a horse, I want to swipe left on geldings so that I can keep my standards.
Bio without thumbs | As a horse, I want to dictate my bio so that 'neeeigh' stops being autocorrected to 'Nigel'.
Verified hoofprint | As a mare, I want verified profiles so that I stop matching with two men in a horse costume.
Rider approval flow | As a rider, I want to approve my horse's matches so that we stop driving to Jutland every weekend.
My good side | As a horse, I want a filter that hides the fly mask so that I look effortless.
Something for Thursday | As a project manager, I want a dashboard of horse matches so that I have something to show on Thursday.
Distance in fields | As a pony, I want distance shown in fields, not km, so that I know if he is worth the trot.
Quiet unmatch | As a stallion, I want to unmatch discreetly so that it is not awkward at the next show.
Horse persona workshop | As a UX designer, I want to interview six horses so that the personas stop being 'Horse A' and 'Horse B'.
The nephew's logo | As the client's nephew, I want to redraw the logo so that it looks more like my horse.
Super Neigh | As a shy Icelandic horse, I want to send a Super Neigh so that he knows I have five gaits.
Consent from every horse | As a data protection officer, I want signed consent so that I can sleep. They sign with a hoof.]]></Value>
    </cardsStory>
    <cardsFeature>
      <Value><![CDATA[Swipe with nose | Touchscreen support for muzzles. The screen protector is now a line item.
Mane filter | Sort by mane: flowing, braided, or 'just woke up in a field'.
Neigh-to-text | Transcribes every voice message as 'neigh'. Accuracy: 100%.
Carrot Boost | Pay one carrot to be shown first in your paddock for 30 minutes.
Location sharing | Shows you as 'in the stable'. You are always in the stable.
It's a Match animation | Confetti made of hay. The designer wants it 2px to the left.
Height in hands | Profiles show height in hands. Everyone adds one hand.
Read receipts | Shows 'seen'. He saw it. He is eating grass. He will keep eating grass.
Blanket status | Blanket on, blanket off, or 'it's complicated'.
Long-distance mode | For horses in different fields. Includes a shared sunset and one fence.
Icebreaker prompts | The default opener: 'Two truths and a neigh'.
Farrier badge | Shows when you last got new shoes. Fresh shoes get 40% more matches.
Group gallop | A group chat for the whole herd. Muted by everyone within the hour.
Push notifications | 'Someone two fields away likes you.' It is the same horse as yesterday.
Jump height slider | Ranges from 'small log' to 'I have seen things'.
Report a donkey | Flag profiles that turn out, on closer inspection, to be a donkey.]]></Value>
    </cardsFeature>
    <cardsBug>
      <Value><![CDATA[Horse matched with itself | Steps: open app near a mirror. Expected: no match. Actual: love. Works on my stable.
Swipe registers as kick | Repro: be a horse. Three test phones lost so far. Severity: yes.
Every profile is the same brown horse | QA cannot tell if this is a bug. Neither can the horses.
Unicorn in production | Nobody created it. It has admin rights. Do not delete, the client loves it.
Every horse is located in Vejle | Some horses really are in Vejle, which makes this very hard to test.
Profile photo is from 2014 | Listed as a glossy three-year-old. Arrived with a grey muzzle and opinions about the old days.
Match email sent to the rider | The rider now knows everything. The horse refuses to make eye contact.
Zebra fails validation | The stripes are read as a barcode. It scans as 'rye bread, 22 kr'.]]></Value>
    </cardsBug>
    <cardsTechdebt>
      <Value><![CDATA[FINAL_v2_real.xlsx | The entire matching engine is one Excel sheet. It lives on a laptop named HORSE-PC.
Hardcoded horse | There is a horse called 'Test Horse' in prod. Removing him breaks login.
jQuery 1.4 | Swiping depends on a plugin last updated when the oldest horse was a foal.
TODO: ask a real horse | A comment from 2019 at the top of the matching algorithm. Still the best spec we have.
No staging stable | All testing happens on live horses. The pipeline is a man with a clipboard and a carrot.
One giant Umbraco node | All profiles live in a single content node called 'Horses (new) (2)'. Do not sort it.]]></Value>
    </cardsTechdebt>
    <cardsCeo>
      <Value><![CDATA[Otto Request: Can it also do AI? | 'Just a little AI. The horses expect it.' Said in the hallway, between two meetings.
Otto Request: Add cows by Friday | 'Same thing, right? Four legs.' No budget, no ticket, big smile.
Otto Request: My horse on the homepage | 'She has a great profile.' The hero image must be replaced before the julefrokost.]]></Value>
    </cardsCeo>
    <siteHeroHeadline>
      <Value><![CDATA[Finally, a stable relationship.]]></Value>
    </siteHeroHeadline>
    <siteHeroSub>
      <Value><![CDATA[The dating app for horses who are tired of meeting the same three ponies in the same field. 100% hooves, 0% thumbs, a surprising number of matches.]]></Value>
    </siteHeroSub>
    <siteCta>
      <Value><![CDATA[Start swiping hooves]]></Value>
    </siteCta>
    <sitePillars>
      <Value><![CDATA[Hoof-first UX | No thumbs? No problem. Every button is 400 px wide and survives a direct kick. Tested in a real stable.
Verified manes | Every profile is checked by a vet. No catfish, and no ponies claiming to be 17 hands.
Matched on hay | Our algorithm pairs on what matters: hay preferences, favourite gait and feelings about trailers.]]></Value>
    </sitePillars>
    <siteTestimonials>
      <Value><![CDATA[I matched with a Shetland from Jutland. We have nothing in common. It's perfect.
Neigh. Five stars. Would neigh again.
My horse now has more dates than I do. I'd like to speak to a project manager.
Onboarding took four minutes and one carrot. Our old system needed a vet.]]></Value>
    </siteTestimonials>
    <sitePricingJoke>
      <Value><![CDATA[Free for horses. Ponies pay per hoof. Riding schools: enterprise, call us for a quote.]]></Value>
    </sitePricingJoke>
    <siteFooterLine>
      <Value><![CDATA[© Tinder for Horses. No horses were consulted. Cookies are sugar lumps and you have already accepted them.]]></Value>
    </siteFooterLine>
